when something happens it is always  you three if you think the golden trio  got dealt a bad hand on screen  wait until you hear what the cast and  crew of harry potter had to deal with  while filming  from serious onset accidents to the  personal struggles of some actors  filming harry potter wasn't always a  casual stroll through hogwarts  what the bloody hell was that all about  it wasn't just harry who had to find a  way to stay underwater for a whole  hour in the goblet of fire daniel  radcliffe had to do it without the help  of neville's gillyweed  in order to get the second task of the  triwizard tournament done  dan trained in huge water tanks for  weeks with professionals so when the  time came he'd be able to do as much  acting as possible underwater but one  day  things went wrong when dan confused some  of the hand signals  who knew a thumbs up could also mean  help i'm literally drowning  it was almost quite frustrating because  the communication is so hard we hear  about how emma watson is literally  hermione in real life but we never talk  about how similar ron and rupert are  especially when it comes to their  playful personalities but rupert's humor  got him into quite a bit of trouble on  set  from day one the actor was prone to  bursting out into laughing fits that had  the entire cast  constantly re-filming the same scenes  over and over  we wouldn't be surprised if rupert ever  pulled a why so serious line as a joke  it might have set the filming back a tad  but it seems like everyone took his  breaking character as a moment to just  laugh things off  sorry just listen to how fondly the  casting crew remember the experience  he just laughs all the time you can't  stop him once he starts  hogwarts might not have been your  ordinary school but they still had to  deal with mundane problems like  lice breakouts while filming the chamber  of secrets the entire cast and crew had  to be checked and treated for life  after they found out some cast members  were infected they were forced to pause  filming for an  entire day while they dealt with all the  cases looks like the basilisk wasn't the  only creature to worry about on set  that year we completely agree with ron's  fear of spiders but we're not gonna lie  light might be the creepy crawly we want  to stay away from  it's disgusting imagine having to go to  school and  work and still getting assigned extra  homework that's what happened to the  golden trio at the start of the prisoner  of azkaban  new director alfonso quaron had the  three young actors write character  essays to make sure they  understood harry hermione and ron  completely they each had to turn in  basically an  autobiography that explained how they  entered the wizarding world and how  their characters have grown  since they were 11. whilst the three of  them seemed oddly okay with the whole  situation  there was something that had dan pretty  annoyed about the whole  essay thing i i felt really so pleased  with myself  we all know filming a movie takes  intense dedication  we're talking hours and hours on set so  can we really blame  13 year old tom felton for sneaking  sweets onto the set for long filming  days  the young actor admitted he used to hide  snacks in the pockets of his robes  during the first films  i don't know i used to stuff a lot of  chocolates and sweets inside the robe  his technique caught on with the other  actors and soon the costume department  was finding  leftover snacks in all of the robes  rumor has it that was the reason the  pockets of the costume robes were sewn  shut in the later films we probably  would have done the same imagine being  tempted by all the prop food that lined  the table of the great hall  ron's right harry you're gonna need your  strength today if you thought watching  the battle of hogwarts unfold in the  deathly hallows was heartbreaking  wait until you find out what happened to  the actual hogwarts set  it burned down for real during the  filming of the deathly hallows one of  the special effects malfunctioned on set  and caused a fire they had been filming  shots at hogwarts but something went  wrong with one of the pyrotechnics  luckily none of the cast was on set when  it happened but they had to rebuild  everything that had gotten destroyed the  damage apparently cost  100 000 euros that's over 120 thousand  dollars  we can't imagine how catastrophic that  must have been such a pity  growing up in the spotlight isn't easy  just ask the entire harry potter cast  whether it be how self-conscious they  were being on camera during puberty or  feeling like they lost their childhood  in some way  almost all the actors have spoken about  the struggle but in dan's case his  struggle with the spotlight turned into  some  unhealthy coping mechanisms during the  filming for a half-blood prince he  suffered from substance abuse  he's admitted that although he never  drank on set he'd still sometimes be  intoxicated when filming rolled around  the next morning it was all because he  was trying to escape the feeling of  being watched  take a look the quickest way of  forgetting about the fact that you were  being watched was to  get very drunk we couldn't imagine  anyone else but emma watson filling the  shoes of hermione granger but there was  a point in time when we might have had  to explore that  in the middle of the franchise emma was  ready to give up her role in harry  potter and it was because her schedule  was totally clashing with her education  she had dreams of going to college and  being hermione was making that extremely  difficult  luckily the producers were able to  figure everything out they did have to  rework her entire filming schedule but  of course  it was worth it in the end she finished  the franchise and graduated from brown  university in 2014  talk about her real-life hermione i  think we had a bad influence on her  walking into the great hall alongside  harry for the first time was  well magical to say the least with its  towering ceiling intimidating  head table and falling candles okay well  we never actually got to see the candles  fall  but they did before they brought the  great halls floating candles to life in  the editing room they tried using real  lit candles but as you've probably  guessed that didn't go too well  the candles burned through the strings  that were supporting them and they fell  on the actor's heads  the only shot they ended up getting with  real candles is the first scene of the  first years walking into the great hall  for the sorting ceremony  in the sorcerer's stone good offender  [Applause]  you'll be pleased to know that the  hogwarts express is a real train and  we're not just talking about the mock  version at universal studios  that means when the production wasn't  using the train it had to be stored at a  depot  for the most part that worked out except  for the two times that it didn't  in 2003 a group of teens spray painted  the outside of the train cars  then in 2007 people went as far as to  smash in the windows of the train  luckily they were able to get it cleaned  and repaired both times so it could get  its moment to shine in each film  our hearts break just thinking about the  train being ruined it's basically an  actual character at this point  it wasn't just the stunt doubles that  got injured on the set of harry potter  while filming the order of the phoenix  neville's actor matthew lewis suffered a  pretty bad injury  while the cast was filming the intense  scene in the ministry of magic  helena bonham carter as bellatrix put  her wand in matthew's ear  matthew happened to move at the same  time she did it and it resulted in him  rupturing his eardrum  of course the whole ordeal was an  accident helena said  i thought i could brandish the wand like  a sort of q-tip sort of  torture it matthew took no hard feelings  for what happened and even tried to  prevent helena from feeling bad by  hiding how bad he was actually hurt  well done daniel radcliffe wasn't the  only actor who suffered mentally during  the filming of the movies devin murray's  character sheamus  was happy and go lucky even if he spent  a lot of his scenes  accidentally blowing things up  but off-screen devin was dealing with  some major depression  it got to the point where his life was  at risk take a listen to what he had to  say about it  i'd gone into the doctors into the  hospital they said they don't know  how long it can last for despite the  mishaps the cast and crew experience  throughout those 10 years we're glad  they were still able to pull through and  create movies that will probably  resonate for generations  they do say everything happens for a  reason if you want more harry potter  videos like this one make sure you hit  that subscribe button  thanks for watching the things
 

